<p class="has-text-align-center has-text-color" style="color:#01824C;margin-bottom:12px;font-family:\'Manrope\', sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.18em">QUESTIONS, ANSWERED</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"style":{"typography":{"fontSize":"44px","fontWeight":"500","lineHeight":"1.08","fontFamily":"\'Cormorant Garamond\', serif","textAlign":"center"},"color":{"text":"#232A20"},"spacing":{"margin":{"bottom":"44px"}}}} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-text-color" style="color:#232A20;margin-bottom:44px;font-family:\'Cormorant Garamond\', serif;font-size:44px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.08">Before you put the kettle on</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"bottom":{"color":"#DDD5C2","width":"1px"}},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"22px","bottom":"22px"}},"color":{"text":"#232a20"},"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#232a20"}}}}} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-text-color has-link-color" style="border-bottom-color:#DDD5C2;border-bottom-width:1px;color:#232a20;padding-top:22px;padding-bottom:22px"><summary>Can I pause or skip a month?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"fontSize":"15px","lineHeight":"1.6","fontFamily":"\'Manrope\', sans-serif"},"color":{"text":"#6A7261"}}} -->
<p class="has-text-color" style="color:#6A7261;font-family:\'Manrope\', sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6">Anytime, with one click from your account — no emails, no phone calls. Your cadence picks back up whenever you are ready, and you keep your subscriber price.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"bottom":{"color":"#DDD5C2","width":"1px"}},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"22px","bottom":"22px"}},"color":{"text":"#232a20"},"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#232a20"}}}}} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-text-color has-link-color" style="border-bottom-color:#DDD5C2;border-bottom-width:1px;color:#232a20;padding-top:22px;padding-bottom:22px"><summary>Is Meadow Rest caffeine-free?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"fontSize":"15px","lineHeight":"1.6","fontFamily":"\'Manrope\', sans-serif"},"color":{"text":"#6A7261"}}} -->
<p class="has-text-color" style="color:#6A7261;font-family:\'Manrope\', sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6">Completely. Chamomile, lemon balm, and oat straw are all naturally caffeine-free herbs, so it is safe to brew right up until bedtime.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"bottom":{"color":"#DDD5C2","width":"1px"}},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"22px","bottom":"22px"}},"color":{"text":"#232a20"},"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#232a20"}}}}} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-text-color has-link-color" style="border-bottom-color:#DDD5C2;border-bottom-width:1px;color:#232a20;padding-top:22px;padding-bottom:22px"><summary>How should I brew it?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"fontSize":"15px","lineHeight":"1.6","fontFamily":"\'Manrope\', sans-serif"},"color":{"text":"#6A7261"}}} -->
<p class="has-text-color" style="color:#6A7261;font-family:\'Manrope\', sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6">One heaped tablespoon per mug, water just off the boil, steeped five to six minutes with a lid on. The lid matters — it keeps the aromatic oils in the cup.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"bottom":{"color":"#DDD5C2","width":"1px"}},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"22px","bottom":"22px"}},"color":{"text":"#232a20"},"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#232a20"}}}}} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-text-color has-link-color" style="border-bottom-color:#DDD5C2;border-bottom-width:1px;color:#232a20;padding-top:22px;padding-bottom:22px"><summary>What happens to the pouches?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"fontSize":"15px","lineHeight":"1.6","fontFamily":"\'Manrope\', sans-serif"},"color":{"text":"#6A7261"}}} -->
<p class="has-text-color" style="color:#6A7261;font-family:\'Manrope\', sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6">They are certified home-compostable, liner and all. Bury one in the garden and it is gone within twelve weeks. The starter tin is yours to refill forever.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details {"style":{"border":{"bottom":{"color":"#DDD5C2","width":"1px"}},"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"22px","bottom":"22px"}},"color":{"text":"#232a20"},"elements":{"link":{"color":{"text":"#232a20"}}}}} -->
<details class="wp-block-details has-text-color has-link-color" style="border-bottom-color:#DDD5C2;border-bottom-width:1px;color:#232a20;padding-top:22px;padding-bottom:22px"><summary>When does my order ship?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"fontSize":"15px","lineHeight":"1.6","fontFamily":"\'Manrope\', sans-serif"},"color":{"text":"#6A7261"}}} -->
<p class="has-text-color" style="color:#6A7261;font-family:\'Manrope\', sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6">Subscriptions blend and ship in the first week of every month. One-time orders leave the farm within two business days.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

